{"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "chunk_id": "ASM-08:rec:ASM-043", "content_sha256": "d0e20b03ed2e7b8531d1731f7998517d82bb10a383e8d43cd82cab41e1fca035", "heading": "ASM-043", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-043", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-043", "text": "### ASM-043 — Industrial-process contexts with named chemistry\n\n**Claim:** the papers frame questions inside real industrial processes, naming\nreagents and catalysts.\n**Evidence:** \"Hydrogen is used to manufacture ammonia, NH3 Hydrogen is reacted with\nnitrogen using an iron catalyst.\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 328-342); \"Ethanol is also manufactured by reacting steam with ethene, C2H4\" with\nthe conditions question \"State the conditions of temperature and pressure used in\nthis process.\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 502-516).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "chunk_id": "ASM-08:rec:ASM-044", "content_sha256": "8a7bbdfaa29eab29dea8ad62b4dad091605f35dfe1ba6b1fec67be90650b6887", "heading": "ASM-044", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-044", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-044", "text": "### ASM-044 — Everyday-application contexts carry structure-property reasoning\n\n**Claim:** familiar objects frame structure-and-bonding explanations.\n**Evidence:** the diamond/graphite uses item — \"diamonds are used in cutting tools ●\ngraphite is used in pencils to make marks on paper\" — demands structure-and-bonding\nreasoning for each use (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-01/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 887-901);\nthe airship frame opens the hydrogen/helium reasoning chain (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 328-342).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "chunk_id": "ASM-08:rec:ASM-045", "content_sha256": "54e4164369f18b2b93df1b4c5b1570b7d210283cbed3a77ae1adee55b82b30cd", "heading": "ASM-045", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-045", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-045", "text": "### ASM-045 — Laboratory-investigation contexts carry the practical strand\n\n**Claim:** investigation contexts (chromatography, evaporation, temperature change,\nrates) frame data-handling and method questions.\n**Evidence:** the chromatography frame \"A student uses this apparatus to investigate\nthe colours in four different inks, A, B, C and D.\" and the\nalcohol-evaporation table investigation .\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "chunk_id": "ASM-08:rec:ASM-046", "content_sha256": "28924922ea5e5418b50d03404fb024cac3389e3fa7b576d8b042b6ae94a6438a", "heading": "ASM-046", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-046", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-046", "text": "### ASM-046 — Materials-engineering contexts\n\n**Claim:** extraction and protection of metals frame electrochemistry and reactivity\nquestions.\n**Evidence:** \"Aluminium is extracted industrially by the electrolysis of molten\naluminium oxide Al2O3\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2021-01/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 306-320)\nand the coating item \"Name the process used to coat iron with zinc.\" with mark\nscheme \"galvanising ACCEPT galvanisation\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-01/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 153-167).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "chunk_id": "ASM-08:rec:ASM-047", "content_sha256": "5ff5f80b5b56dc2f20b4a629f14df27b27d377501bff0a67e7d42a730128072a", "heading": "ASM-047", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-047", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-047", "text": "### ASM-047 — Staged-manufacture narratives chain reactions\n\n**Claim:** multi-stage narratives present consecutive reactions as one question\nframe.\n**Evidence:** \"Nitric acid (HNO3) is used in the production of fertilisers. Nitric\nacid is manufactured in three stages.\" with Stage 1 ammonia-oxidation chemistry\nprinted in the stem (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-01/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 1094-1108);\nthe two-stage chloroethene process \"Ethene (C2H4) can be converted into\nchloroethene (C2H3Cl) in a two-stage process.\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 563-577).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "chunk_id": "ASM-08:rec:ASM-048", "content_sha256": "b2b953983c682b52e308a23c593d552dc7eb75471eb789e213fba0826914e8fd", "heading": "ASM-048", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-08", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-048", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-048", "text": "### ASM-048 — The constant: new context, core chemistry\n\n**Claim:** across all context families the tested demand stays on specification-core\napplication — conditions, properties, equations — rather than contextual trivia.\n**Evidence:** the ammonia frame asks for the standard catalyst-rate reasoning\n(\"State why a catalyst is used in this reaction.\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 386-400) with the rate/activation-energy\nmark scheme, SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 386-400); the\nethanol frame asks the standard conditions; the polymer frame asks for the polymer\nname from the monomer .\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
